        "text": "To find the general antiderivative, we must consider each part of the expression separately.\n\nFor the first term, 7x^3, identify the exponent n.\nDetermine the value of (n + 1) to use as both the multiplier and the denominator.\nApply this to the first term: (3 + 1) * x^(3+1) / (3 + 1).\nFor the second term, 5x, identify the exponent n.\nDetermine the value of (n + 1) for the second term.\nApply this to the second term: (1 + 1) * x^(1+1) / (1 + 1).",
