        "mastery": 0.0,
        "prior_failures": 3,
        "text": "You're right that the specific number doesn't change how the function behaves in many cases. However, since we have no way of knowing if the original constant was 5, 100, or 0, what would happen to our claim of accuracy if we just picked one and left it out?",
